# Desired CPU socket power limit (PPT) in milliwatts, re-asserted at every boot by
# hsmp-control-apply.service. Accepted window: 100000..300000 mW (same as openfan-linux's CPU control).
#
# This is a runtime HSMP setting, not the BIOS value. The SMU limit is volatile: after a reboot
# firmware re-programs it from CBS (visible as "PPT (BIOS default, flash)" in `limits`), which
# is exactly why this file and the unit exist. Changing the BIOS default itself requires Setup —
# this firmware refuses OS-runtime writes to that variable while Secure Boot is enabled.
#
# The first non-comment line wins. Absent file or absent service means "no override wanted":
# the limit stays wherever CBS put it.

290000
